From: Package maintainers <packages@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] layer libva.conf across administrator, runtime, and vendor
Source: downstream
Upstream: not submitted; suitable for upstream review

va_parseConfig() only opens SYSCONFDIR "/libva.conf". Meson compiles
SYSCONFDIR as "/etc" whenever prefix is "/usr", so this reader never
consults a runtime or vendor file, and a shipped copy of libva can only
carry its default LIBVA_MESSAGING_LEVEL and LIBVA_TRACE* settings by
writing directly into the administrator's /etc.

Try the administrator file, then a runtime file, then a vendor file, and
stop at the first one that opens. A file that opens but does not contain
the requested key still falls through to the environment exactly as
before, so an existing higher-priority file, even an empty one, masks
every lower file without ever being read again. Nothing else in
va_parseConfig changes: a value found in the selected file still beats
the process environment.

diff -urN a/va/va.c b/va/va.c
--- a/va/va.c
+++ b/va/va.c
@@ -81,14 +81,24 @@
  */
 int va_parseConfig(char *env, char *env_value)
 {
+    static const char *const va_config_paths[] = {
+        SYSCONFDIR "/libva.conf",
+        "/run/libva.conf",
+        "/usr/lib/libva.conf",
+    };
     char *token, *value, *saveptr;
     char oneline[1024];
     FILE *fp = NULL;
+    unsigned int i;

     if (env == NULL)
         return 1;

-    fp = fopen(SYSCONFDIR "/libva.conf", "r");
+    for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(va_config_paths); i++) {
+        fp = fopen(va_config_paths[i], "r");
+        if (fp)
+            break;
+    }
     while (fp && (fgets(oneline, 1024, fp) != NULL)) {
         if (strlen(oneline) == 1)
             continue;
